// Language server main loop: same parse and check as `j3c`, stdio JSON-RPC (Content-Length framing).
//
// Port of: j3c/src/lsp/mod.rs
// J3: A handler table on the shared JSON-RPC loop in `lsp/proto` (plan 11 B12.4); parts `lsp/handlers.j3` (the
// request handlers) and `lsp/reply.j3` (capabilities, replies). Each recheck is a fresh `driver.Session`
// (`lsp.query.analyze`) keyed on the open buffers in uri order; the old one is freed when the new one replaces
// it (B6). The wave-25 probe ran 1000 Session create/check/free cycles inside j3c-boot (split build) with flat
// RSS, so no arena reuse is needed (contracts-c5.md). Gate: 1000 `didChange` edits of one buffer, RSS levels off.
// J3: Unlike Rust, an unknown method gets -32601 and a bad JSON body -32700 (`lsp/proto`); neither is in a
// byte-compared session.
// J3: Deferred (user, 2026-11-18): not ported yet; stubs keep their signatures. See plans/06-deferred-tools.md.
module j3c.lsp;
